------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <DataTableResizer> is a PURE presentational PRIMITIVE. Its inputs are plain props (columnKey,
width, minWidth, maxWidth, onResize, onResizeEnd, label) and it renders a drag handle that reports widths
back through callbacks. There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise -> therefore NO loading /
error / stale / offline branch (there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect from; the hosting
<th> owns its own data states; the component has no hooks at all). Reproducing those generic states would
FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so this surface reproduces only the source's REAL branches —
exactly the disposition the accepted sibling presentational primitives DataTableBulkBar (0209), Accordion
(0203), ActiveFilterChips (0147), InlineCallout (0124), Delta (0081), MetricCard (0095), and StaggerItem
(0194) used. The REAL branches, all reproduced + previewed + tested:
  • resting          : opacity-0 — the bar is invisible until interaction (web resizer base class).
  • hover            : opacity-100 + cyan/40 tint (web `hover:bg-cyan-400/40`).
  • focus (keyboard) : opacity-100 + cyan/60 tint (web `focus-visible:bg-cyan-400/60`).
  • dragging         : opacity-100 + cyan/60 tint (web `dragging && 'bg-cyan-400/60'`).
  • clamp floor/ceil : width pinned to minWidth / maxWidth (web `clamp` = Math.max(min, Math.min(max, …))).
  • keyboard splitter: ArrowLeft/Right ±8, Home→80, End→maxWidth (web key handler; both onResize+onResizeEnd).
Data source  : none (pure presentational; width is a caller-supplied controlled prop, not fetched).
Shared comps : none (the web source uses none).
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : the web source is ANONYMOUS — it builds `label ?? \`Resize column ${columnKey}\`` inline and
               exposes the width via `aria-valuenow`, calling no t(). The native VoiceOver additions
               table.resizer.label ("Resize column {{column}}"), table.resizer.value ("{{width}} points"),
               table.resizer.hint ("Drag, or use the arrow keys, to resize the column") all resolve through
               the P1/S10 facade; no English literals in code.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "DataTableResizer" (P1/S11).
a11y         : the WAI-ARIA "Window Splitter" pattern (web role="separator" + aria-valuenow/min/max +
               tabIndex=0 + arrow-key resize) maps to a native accessible element with an adjustable action
               — VoiceOver announces the resize label + the "{{width}} points" value, a swipe up/down
               grows/shrinks the column (increment->ArrowRight, decrement->ArrowLeft), and the hint
               narrates the gesture. .focusable() supplies the keyboard focus the splitter needs; the macOS
               column-resize cursor mirrors web `cursor-col-resize`; the tint fade honors Reduce Motion.

